# Qt 6 dependencies as alternatives, because the package name differs between
# the distributions this package claims to target and dpkg-shlibdeps can only
# know the one it is building on.
#
# Ubuntu 24.04 carried out the 64-bit time_t transition by renaming the
# affected runtime packages with a "t64" suffix. Debian 13 did the transition
# too but did not rename every package, and the two do not agree on which:
#
#   libQt6Core     libqt6core6t64      exists on both
#   libQt6Gui      libqt6gui6t64       Ubuntu only -- Debian 13 has libqt6gui6
#   libQt6Widgets  libqt6widgets6t64   Ubuntu only -- Debian 13 has libqt6widgets6
#
# So a .deb built on Ubuntu 24.04 declared two dependencies with no candidate
# on Debian 13, and apt refused it outright: "libqt6gui6t64 but it is not
# installable". Verified against a Debian 13 host before and after this file.
#
# An alternative satisfies whichever name the target actually has, which is
# what a package spanning both wants. The versions match what dpkg-shlibdeps
# derives from Qt's own shlibs on Ubuntu 24.04; the Debian names carry the same
# minimums because the ABI they refer to is the same.
libQt6Core 6 libqt6core6t64 (>= 6.4.0) | libqt6core6 (>= 6.4.0)
libQt6Gui 6 libqt6gui6t64 (>= 6.1.2) | libqt6gui6 (>= 6.1.2)
libQt6Widgets 6 libqt6widgets6t64 (>= 6.3.0) | libqt6widgets6 (>= 6.3.0)
